# promise: #407
# Arc Max's Instant Links (Arc 1.172.2, live with Max on, 12 Nov 2026): Shift-Return on a search in ⌘T
# makes the model plan the phrase, searches Google in a page nobody sees and opens the top results.
# While it works the sidebar shows "Searching the web for you…" at the top of Today, drawn as the open
# row when the run came from ⌘T's new-tab bar; the results then replace it. Tabs open at the top of
# Today in result order with the first selected; a split lands at the top of Today; a folder of one
# search opens 5 pages at the end of Pinned, named by the plan. When nothing can be opened the row reads
# "Oops, something went wrong." until its ✕ is pressed (cra://debug?instantLinksDismiss=1 here). Cra
# goes past Arc in two places: the stated count is honoured, and a model that throws (a guardrail's false
# positive, a language it doesn't speak) falls back to searching the phrase as typed, where Arc shows the
# error. With the setting off Shift-Return is a plain Return. The model is Cra's test model, the
# search is the fixture page shaped like Google's results (CRA_INSTANT_LINKS_SEARCH).
budget rss=900 stalls50=30 perfcpu=0.5
pace 0.5
port 8765
env CRA_TIDY_FAKE_MODEL=1
env CRA_INSTANT_LINKS_SEARCH=http://127.0.0.1:8765/instant-links.html?q={searchTerms}
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "instantLinks": true}

cra://open?url=${PAGE}
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
# Cra makes a spare page 1 s after the last page (SparePages); let it be made before the bar opens,
# or the scripted Return can miss the bar in this background copy.
wait 2
cra://debug?instantLinks=before
expect-log Cra instant links before: available=true rows=0 status=- current=0 plan=- opened=- fellback=0 today=\[x\*\] pinned=\[\]$

# Shift-Return: the row stands for the new tab ⌘T was opening, and is replaced by three tabs at the
# top of Today, in result order, the first selected (the open page moves down).
cra://commandbar?query=top%203%20pizza%20places%20in%20naples
wait 1
cra://debug?key=%0D,36,131072
wait 0.5
cra://debug?instantLinks=working
expect-log Cra instant links working: available=true rows=1 status=loading current=1 plan=- opened=-
wait 6
cra://debug?instantLinks=tabs
expect-log Cra instant links tabs: available=true rows=0 status=- current=0 plan=tab/1/3 opened=3 fellback=0 today=\[1\*,2,3,x\] pinned=\[\]$

# A split of three results: one row at the top of Today, the first pane selected.
cra://commandbar?query=top%203%20greek%20restaurants%20in%20a%20split
wait 1
cra://debug?key=%0D,36,131072
wait 6
cra://debug?instantLinks=split
expect-log Cra instant links split: .*plan=split/1/3 opened=3 fellback=0 today=\[1\*\+2\+3,1,2,3,x\] pinned=\[\]$

# A folder of one search opens 5 pages (Arc's rule) at the end of Pinned, named by the plan, and
# nothing is added to Today; the first page, inside it, is the selected one. A second folder goes after the first.
cra://commandbar?query=folder%20of%20pizza
wait 1
cra://debug?key=%0D,36,131072
wait 6
cra://debug?instantLinks=folder
expect-log Cra instant links folder: .*plan=folder/1/5 opened=5 .*today=\[1\+2\+3,1,2,3,x\] pinned=\["Pizza"\{1\*,2,3,4,5\}\]$
cra://commandbar?query=folder%20of%20pasta
wait 1
cra://debug?key=%0D,36,131072
wait 6
cra://debug?instantLinks=folders
expect-log Cra instant links folders: .*pinned=\["Pizza"\{1,2,3,4,5\},"Pasta"\{1\*,2,3,4,5\}\]$

# Nothing could be opened: the row turns into the error, stays until dismissed, and opens nothing.
cra://debug?instantLinksFail=plan
cra://commandbar?query=top%203%20pizza%20places
wait 1
cra://debug?key=%0D,36,131072
wait 4
cra://debug?instantLinks=error
expect-log Cra instant links error: available=true rows=1 status=error current=1 plan=- opened=-
cra://debug?instantLinksDismiss=1
cra://debug?instantLinks=dismissed
expect-log Cra instant links dismissed: available=true rows=0 status=-

# The model throws (a guardrail's false positive, say): the phrase is searched as typed, with its
# stated count, and the results open as tabs. Only the failure's kind is logged.
cra://debug?instantLinksFail=model
cra://commandbar?query=top%202%20youtube%20mkbhd
wait 1
cra://debug?key=%0D,36,131072
wait 6
cra://debug?instantLinks=fallback
expect-log Instant Links: the model failed \(test\); searching the phrase as typed
expect-log Cra instant links fallback: available=true rows=0 status=- current=0 plan=tab/1/2 opened=2 fellback=1 today=\[1\*,2,1\+2\+3,1,2,3,x\]

# With the setting off Shift-Return is a plain Return: no row, no run.
cra://debug?instantLinksFail=none
cra://debug?instantLinksSetting=off
cra://commandbar?query=top%203%20pizza%20places
wait 1
cra://debug?key=%0D,36,131072
wait 2
cra://debug?instantLinks=off
expect-log Cra instant links off: available=false rows=0 status=- current=0 plan=tab/1/2 opened=2 fellback=1 today=\[x\*,1,2,1\+2\+3,
